NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Solid Query is written in "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TypeScript"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to make sure the library and your projects are type-safe!"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Things to keep in mind:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Query follows "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped#support-window","children":[{"type":"text","value":"DefinitelyTyped's support window"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and supports TypeScript versions released within the last 2 years. At the moment, that means TypeScript "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"5.6"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and newer."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Changes to types in this repository are considered "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"non-breaking"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and are usually released as "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"patch"}]},{"type":"text","value":" semver changes (otherwise every type enhancement would be a major version!)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It is "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"highly recommended that you lock your solid-query package version to a specific patch release and upgrade with the expectation that types may be fixed or upgraded between any release"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The non-type-related public API of Solid Query still follows semver very strictly."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-inference","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Inference"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Types in Solid Query generally flow through very well so that you don't have to provide type annotations for yourself"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useQuery } from '@tanstack/solid-query'\n\nconst query = useQuery(() => ({\n  queryKey: ['number'],\n  queryFn: () => Promise.resolve(5),\n}))\n\nquery.data\n//    ^? (property) data: number | undefined","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://www.typescriptlang.org/play/?#code/JYWwDg9gTgLgBAbzgYygUwIYzQRQK5pQCecAvnAGZQQhwDkAAjBgHYDOzyA1gPRsQAbYABMAtAEcCxOgFgAUPOQR28SYRIBeFOiy4pRABQGAlHA0A+OAYTy4duGuIBpNEQBccANp0WeEACNCOgBdABo4W3tHIgAxFg8TM0sABWoQYDY0ADp0fgEANzQDAFZjeVJjMoU5aKzhLAx5Hh57OAA9AH55brkgA","children":[{"type":"text","value":"typescript playground"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { useQuery } from '@tanstack/solid-query'\n\nconst query = useQuery(() => ({\n  queryKey: ['test'],\n  queryFn: () => Promise.resolve(5),\n  select: (data) => data.toString(),\n}))\n\nquery.data\n//    ^? (property) data: string | undefined","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://www.typescriptlang.org/play/?#code/JYWwDg9gTgLgBAbzgYygUwIYzQRQK5pQCecAvnAGZQQhwDkAAjBgHYDOzyA1gPRsQAbYABMAtAEcCxOgFgAUPOQR28SYRIBeFOiy4pRABQGAlHA0A+OAYTy4duGuIBpNEQBccANp1sHOgF0AGjhbe0ciADEWDxMzSwAFahBgNjQAOnR+AQA3NAMAVmNA0LtUgTRkGBjhLAxTCzga5jSYCABlGChgFgBzE2K5UmNjeXlwtKaMeR4eezgAPQB+UYU5IA","children":[{"type":"text","value":"typescript playground"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This works best if your "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryFn"},{"type":"text","value":" has a well-defined returned type. Keep in mind that most data fetching libraries return "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"any"},{"type":"text","value":" per default, so make sure to extract it to a properly typed function:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const fetchGroups = (): Promise<Group[]> =>\n  axios.get('/groups').then((response) => response.data)\n\nconst query = useQuery(() => ({\n  queryKey: ['groups'],\n  queryFn: fetchGroups,\n}))\n\nquery.data\n//    ^? (property) data: Group[] | undefined","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://www.typescriptlang.org/play/?ssl=11&ssc=4&pln=6&pc=1#code/JYWwDg9gTgLgBAbzgYygUwIYzQRQK5pQCecAvnAGZQQhwDkAAjBgHYDOzyA1gPRsQAbYABMAtAEcCxOgFgAUKEiw4GAB7AIbStVp01GtrLnyYRMGjgBxanjBwAvIjgiAXHBZ4QAI0Jl585Ah2eAo0GGQAC2sIWy1HAAoASjcABR1gNjQAHmjbAG0AXQA+BxL9TQA6AHMw+LoeKpswQ0SKmAi0Fnj0Nkh2C3sSnr7MiuEsDET-OUDguElCEkdUTGx8Rfik0rh4hHk4A-mpIgBpNCI3PLpGmOa6AoAaOH3DheIAMRY3UPCoprYHvJSIkpsY5G8iGMJvIeDxDnAAHoAfmm8iAA","children":[{"type":"text","value":"typescript playground"}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-narrowing","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Narrowing"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Solid Query uses a "},{"type":"link","href":"https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/typescript-in-5-minutes-func.html#discriminated-unions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"discriminated union type"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the query result, discriminated by the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"status"},{"type":"text","value":" field and the derived status boolean flags. This will allow you to check for e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"success"},{"type":"text","value":" status to make "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data"},{"type":"text","value":" defined:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const query = useQuery(() => ({\n  queryKey: ['number'],\n  queryFn: () => Promise.resolve(5),\n}))\n\nif (query.isSuccess) {\n  const data = query.data\n  //     ^? const data: number\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://www.typescriptlang.org/play/?#code/JYWwDg9gTgLgBAbzgYygUwIYzQRQK5pQCecAvnAGZQQhwDkAAjBgHYDOzyA1gPRsQAbYABMAtAEcCxOgFgAUKEixEKdFjQBRChTTJ45KjXr8hYgFZtZc+cgjt4kwiQC8qzNnxOAFF4CUcZwA+OC8EeTg4R2IAaTQiAC44AG06FjwQACNCOgBdABpwyKkiADEWRL8A4IAFahBgNjQAOnQTADc0LwBWXwK5Ul9feXlgChCooiaGgGU8ZGQ0NjZ-MLkIiNt7OGEsDACipyad5kKInh51iIA9AH55UmHrOSA","children":[{"type":"text","value":"typescript playground"}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"typing-the-error-field","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Typing the error field"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The type for error defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Error"},{"type":"text","value":", because that is what most users expect."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const query = useQuery(() => ({\n  queryKey: ['groups'],\n  queryFn: fetchGroups,\n}))\n\nquery.error\n//    ^? (property) error: Error | null","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://www.typescriptlang.org/play/?#code/JYWwDg9gTgLgBAbzgYygUwIYzQRQK5pQCecAvnAGZQQhwDkAAjBgHYDOzyA1gPRsQAbYABMAtAEcCxOgFgAUKEiw4GAB7AIbStVp01GtrLnyYRMGjgBxanjBwAvIjgiAXHBZ4QAI0Jl585Ah2eAo0GGQAC2sIWy1HAAoASjcABR1gNjQAHmjbAG0AXQA+BxL9TQA6AHMw+LoeKpswQ0SKmAi0Fnj0Nkh2C3sSnr7MiuEsDET-OUDguElCEkdUTGx8Rfik0rh4hHk4A-mpIgBpNCI3PLpGmOa6AoAaOH3DheIAMRY3UPCoprYHvJSIkpsY5G8iBVCNQoPIeDxDnAAHoAfmm8iAA","children":[{"type":"text","value":"typescript playground"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you want to throw a custom error, or something that isn't an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Error"},{"type":"text","value":" at all, you can specify the type of the error field:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const query = useQuery<Group[], string>(() => ({\n  queryKey: ['groups'],\n  queryFn: fetchGroups,\n}))\n\nquery.error\n//    ^? (property) error: string | null","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"However, this has the drawback that type inference for all other generics of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useQuery"},{"type":"text","value":" will not work anymore. It is generally not considered a good practice to throw something that isn't an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Error"},{"type":"text","value":", so if you have a subclass like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AxiosError"},{"type":"text","value":" you can use "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"type narrowing"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to make the error field more specific:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import axios from 'axios'\n\nconst query = useQuery(() => ({\n  queryKey: ['groups'],\n  queryFn: fetchGroups,\n}))\n\nquery.error\n//    ^? (property) error: Error | null\n\nif (axios.isAxiosError(query.error)) {\n  query.error\n  //    ^? (property) error: AxiosError\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://www.typescriptlang.org/play/?#code/JYWwDg9gTgLgBAbzgYygUwIYzQRQK5pQCecAvnAGZQQhwDkAAjBgHYDOzyA1gPRsQAbYABMAtAEcCxOgFgAUKEiw4GAB7AIbStVp01GtrLnyYRMGjgBxanjBwAvIjgiAXHBZ4QAI0Jl585Ah2eAo0GGQAC2sIWy1HAAoASjcABR1gNjQAHmjbAG0AXQA+BxL9TQA6AHMw+LoeKpswQ0SKmAi0Fnj0Nkh2C3sSnr7MiuEsDET-OUDguElCEkdUTGx8Rfik0rh4hHk4A-mpIgBpNCI3PLpGmOa6AoAaOH3DheIAMRY3UPCoprYHvJSIkpsY5G8iBVCNQoPIeDxDnAAHoAfmmwAoO3KbAqGQAgupNABRKAw+IQqGk6AgxAvA4U6HQOlweGI1FA+RAA","children":[{"type":"text","value":"typescript playground"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"import '@tanstack/solid-query'\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/solid-query' {\n  interface Register {\n    // Use unknown so call sites must narrow explicitly.\n    defaultError: unknown\n  }\n}\n\nconst query = useQuery(() => ({\n  queryKey: ['groups'],\n  queryFn: fetchGroups,\n}))\n\nquery.error\n//    ^? (property) error: unknown | null","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"registering-global-meta","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Registering global "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Meta"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Similarly to registering a "},{"type":"link","href":"#registering-a-global-error","children":[{"type":"text","value":"global error type"}]},{"type":"text","value":" you can also register a global "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Meta"},{"type":"text","value":" type. This ensures the optional "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"meta"},{"type":"text","value":" field on "},{"type":"link","href":"./reference/functions/useQuery.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"queries"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"link","href":"./reference/functions/useMutation.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"mutations"}]},{"type":"text","value":" stays consistent and is type-safe. Note that the registered type must extend "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Record<string, unknown>"},{"type":"text","value":" so that "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"meta"},{"type":"text","value":" remains an object."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import '@tanstack/solid-query'\n\ninterface MyMeta extends Record<string, unknown> {\n  // Your meta type definition.\n}\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/solid-query' {\n  interface Register {\n    queryMeta: MyMeta\n    mutationMeta: MyMeta\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"typing-query-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Typing Query Options"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you inline query options into "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useQuery"},{"type":"text","value":", you'll get automatic type inference. However, you might want to extract the query options into a separate function to share them between "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useQuery"},{"type":"text","value":" and e.g "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"query"},{"type":"text","value":". In that case, you'd lose type inference. To get it back, you can use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" helper:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { queryOptions } from '@tanstack/solid-query'\n\nfunction groupOptions() {\n  return queryOptions({\n    queryKey: ['groups'],\n    queryFn: fetchGroups,\n    staleTime: 5 * 1000,\n  })\n}\n\nuseQuery(groupOptions)\nqueryClient.query(groupOptions())","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Further, the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryKey"},{"type":"text","value":" returned from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryOptions"},{"type":"text","value":" knows about the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryFn"},{"type":"text","value":" associated with it, and we can leverage that type information to make functions like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryClient.getQueryData"},{"type":"text","value":" aware of those types as well:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"function groupOptions() {\n  return queryOptions({\n    queryKey: ['groups'],\n    queryFn: fetchGroups,\n    staleTime: 5 * 1000,\n  })\n}\n\nconst data = queryClient.getQueryData(groupOptions().queryKey)\n//    ^? const data: Group[] | undefined","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Without "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryOptions"},{"type":"text","value":", the type of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data"},{"type":"text","value":" would be "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"},{"type":"text","value":", unless we'd pass a generic to it:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const data = queryClient.getQueryData<Group[]>(['groups'])","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"typesafe-disabling-of-queries-using-skiptoken","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Typesafe disabling of queries using "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"skipToken"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you are using TypeScript, you can use the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"skipToken"},{"type":"text","value":" to disable a query. This is useful when you want to disable a query based on a condition, but you still want to keep the query to be type safe."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read more about it in the "},{"type":"link","href":"./guides/disabling-queries.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Disabling Queries"}]},{"type":"text","value":" guide."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"type-inference","text":"Type Inference","level":2},{"id":"type-narrowing","text":"Type Narrowing","level":2},{"id":"typing-the-error-field","text":"Typing the error field","level":2},{"id":"registering-global-meta","text":"Registering global Meta","level":2},{"id":"typing-query-options","text":"Typing Query Options","level":2},{"id":"typesafe-disabling-of-queries-using-skiptoken","text":"Typesafe disabling of queries using skipToken","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nSolid Query is written in **TypeScript** to make sure the library and your projects are type-safe!\n\nThings to keep in mind:\n\n- TanStack Query follows [DefinitelyTyped's support window](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped#support-window) and supports TypeScript versions released within the last 2 years. At the moment, that means TypeScript **5.6** and newer.\n- Changes to types in this repository are considered **non-breaking** and are usually released as **patch** semver changes (otherwise every type enhancement would be a major version!).\n- It is **highly recommended that you lock your solid-query package version to a specific patch release and upgrade with the expectation that types may be fixed or upgraded between any release**\n- The non-type-related public API of Solid Query still follows semver very strictly.\n\n## Type Inference\n\nTypes in Solid Query generally flow through very well so that you don't have to provide type annotations for yourself\n\n```tsx\nimport { useQuery } from '@tanstack/solid-query'\n\nconst query = useQuery(() => ({\n  queryKey: ['number'],\n  queryFn: () => Promise.resolve(5),\n}))\n\nquery.data\n//    ^? (property) data: number | undefined\n```\n\n[typescript playground](https://www.typescriptlang.org/play/?#code/JYWwDg9gTgLgBAbzgYygUwIYzQRQK5pQCecAvnAGZQQhwDkAAjBgHYDOzyA1gPRsQAbYABMAtAEcCxOgFgAUPOQR28SYRIBeFOiy4pRABQGAlHA0A+OAYTy4duGuIBpNEQBccANp0WeEACNCOgBdABo4W3tHIgAxFg8TM0sABWoQYDY0ADp0fgEANzQDAFZjeVJjMoU5aKzhLAx5Hh57OAA9AH55brkgA)\n\n```tsx\nimport { useQuery } from '@tanstack/solid-query'\n\nconst query = useQuery(() => ({\n  queryKey: ['test'],\n  queryFn: () => Promise.resolve(5),\n  select: (data) => data.toString(),\n}))\n\nquery.data\n//    ^? (property) data: string | undefined\n```\n\n[typescript playground](https://www.typescriptlang.org/play/?#code/JYWwDg9gTgLgBAbzgYygUwIYzQRQK5pQCecAvnAGZQQhwDkAAjBgHYDOzyA1gPRsQAbYABMAtAEcCxOgFgAUPOQR28SYRIBeFOiy4pRABQGAlHA0A+OAYTy4duGuIBpNEQBccANp1sHOgF0AGjhbe0ciADEWDxMzSwAFahBgNjQAOnR+AQA3NAMAVmNA0LtUgTRkGBjhLAxTCzga5jSYCABlGChgFgBzE2K5UmNjeXlwtKaMeR4eezgAPQB+UYU5IA)\n\nThis works best if your `queryFn` has a well-defined returned type. Keep in mind that most data fetching libraries return `any` per default, so make sure to extract it to a properly typed function:\n\n```tsx\nconst fetchGroups = (): Promise<Group[]> =>\n  axios.get('/groups').then((response) => response.data)\n\nconst query = useQuery(() => ({\n  queryKey: ['groups'],\n  queryFn: fetchGroups,\n}))\n\nquery.data\n//    ^? (property) data: Group[] | undefined\n```\n\n[typescript playground](https://www.typescriptlang.org/play/?ssl=11&ssc=4&pln=6&pc=1#code/JYWwDg9gTgLgBAbzgYygUwIYzQRQK5pQCecAvnAGZQQhwDkAAjBgHYDOzyA1gPRsQAbYABMAtAEcCxOgFgAUKEiw4GAB7AIbStVp01GtrLnyYRMGjgBxanjBwAvIjgiAXHBZ4QAI0Jl585Ah2eAo0GGQAC2sIWy1HAAoASjcABR1gNjQAHmjbAG0AXQA+BxL9TQA6AHMw+LoeKpswQ0SKmAi0Fnj0Nkh2C3sSnr7MiuEsDET-OUDguElCEkdUTGx8Rfik0rh4hHk4A-mpIgBpNCI3PLpGmOa6AoAaOH3DheIAMRY3UPCoprYHvJSIkpsY5G8iGMJvIeDxDnAAHoAfmm8iAA)\n\n## Type Narrowing\n\nSolid Query uses a [discriminated union type](https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/typescript-in-5-minutes-func.html#discriminated-unions) for the query result, discriminated by the `status` field and the derived status boolean flags. This will allow you to check for e.g. `success` status to make `data` defined:\n\n```tsx\nconst query = useQuery(() => ({\n  queryKey: ['number'],\n  queryFn: () => Promise.resolve(5),\n}))\n\nif (query.isSuccess) {\n  const data = query.data\n  //     ^? const data: number\n}\n```\n\n[typescript playground](https://www.typescriptlang.org/play/?#code/JYWwDg9gTgLgBAbzgYygUwIYzQRQK5pQCecAvnAGZQQhwDkAAjBgHYDOzyA1gPRsQAbYABMAtAEcCxOgFgAUKEixEKdFjQBRChTTJ45KjXr8hYgFZtZc+cgjt4kwiQC8qzNnxOAFF4CUcZwA+OC8EeTg4R2IAaTQiAC44AG06FjwQACNCOgBdABpwyKkiADEWRL8A4IAFahBgNjQAOnQTADc0LwBWXwK5Ul9feXlgChCooiaGgGU8ZGQ0NjZ-MLkIiNt7OGEsDACipyad5kKInh51iIA9AH55UmHrOSA)\n\n## Typing the error field\n\nThe type for error defaults to `Error`, because that is what most users expect.\n\n```tsx\nconst query = useQuery(() => ({\n  queryKey: ['groups'],\n  queryFn: fetchGroups,\n}))\n\nquery.error\n//    ^? (property) error: Error | null\n```\n\n[typescript playground](https://www.typescriptlang.org/play/?#code/JYWwDg9gTgLgBAbzgYygUwIYzQRQK5pQCecAvnAGZQQhwDkAAjBgHYDOzyA1gPRsQAbYABMAtAEcCxOgFgAUKEiw4GAB7AIbStVp01GtrLnyYRMGjgBxanjBwAvIjgiAXHBZ4QAI0Jl585Ah2eAo0GGQAC2sIWy1HAAoASjcABR1gNjQAHmjbAG0AXQA+BxL9TQA6AHMw+LoeKpswQ0SKmAi0Fnj0Nkh2C3sSnr7MiuEsDET-OUDguElCEkdUTGx8Rfik0rh4hHk4A-mpIgBpNCI3PLpGmOa6AoAaOH3DheIAMRY3UPCoprYHvJSIkpsY5G8iBVCNQoPIeDxDnAAHoAfmm8iAA)\n\nIf you want to throw a custom error, or something that isn't an `Error` at all, you can specify the type of the error field:\n\n```tsx\nconst query = useQuery<Group[], string>(() => ({\n  queryKey: ['groups'],\n  queryFn: fetchGroups,\n}))\n\nquery.error\n//    ^? (property) error: string | null\n```\n\nHowever, this has the drawback that type inference for all other generics of `useQuery` will not work anymore. It is generally not considered a good practice to throw something that isn't an `Error`, so if you have a subclass like `AxiosError` you can use _type narrowing_ to make the error field more specific:\n\n```tsx\nimport axios from 'axios'\n\nconst query = useQuery(() => ({\n  queryKey: ['groups'],\n  queryFn: fetchGroups,\n}))\n\nquery.error\n//    ^? (property) error: Error | null\n\nif (axios.isAxiosError(query.error)) {\n  query.error\n  //    ^? (property) error: AxiosError\n}\n```\n\n[typescript playground](https://www.typescriptlang.org/play/?#code/JYWwDg9gTgLgBAbzgYygUwIYzQRQK5pQCecAvnAGZQQhwDkAAjBgHYDOzyA1gPRsQAbYABMAtAEcCxOgFgAUKEiw4GAB7AIbStVp01GtrLnyYRMGjgBxanjBwAvIjgiAXHBZ4QAI0Jl585Ah2eAo0GGQAC2sIWy1HAAoASjcABR1gNjQAHmjbAG0AXQA+BxL9TQA6AHMw+LoeKpswQ0SKmAi0Fnj0Nkh2C3sSnr7MiuEsDET-OUDguElCEkdUTGx8Rfik0rh4hHk4A-mpIgBpNCI3PLpGmOa6AoAaOH3DheIAMRY3UPCoprYHvJSIkpsY5G8iBVCNQoPIeDxDnAAHoAfmmwAoO3KbAqGQAgupNABRKAw+IQqGk6AgxAvA4U6HQOlweGI1FA+RAA)\n\n[//]: # 'RegisterErrorType'\n\n```tsx\nimport '@tanstack/solid-query'\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/solid-query' {\n  interface Register {\n    // Use unknown so call sites must narrow explicitly.\n    defaultError: unknown\n  }\n}\n\nconst query = useQuery(() => ({\n  queryKey: ['groups'],\n  queryFn: fetchGroups,\n}))\n\nquery.error\n//    ^? (property) error: unknown | null\n```\n\n[//]: # 'RegisterErrorType'\n\n## Registering global `Meta`\n\nSimilarly to registering a [global error type](#registering-a-global-error) you can also register a global `Meta` type. This ensures the optional `meta` field on [queries](./reference/functions/useQuery.md) and [mutations](./reference/functions/useMutation.md) stays consistent and is type-safe. Note that the registered type must extend `Record<string, unknown>` so that `meta` remains an object.\n\n```ts\nimport '@tanstack/solid-query'\n\ninterface MyMeta extends Record<string, unknown> {\n  // Your meta type definition.\n}\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/solid-query' {\n  interface Register {\n    queryMeta: MyMeta\n    mutationMeta: MyMeta\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Typing Query Options\n\nIf you inline query options into `useQuery`, you'll get automatic type inference. However, you might want to extract the query options into a separate function to share them between `useQuery` and e.g `query`. In that case, you'd lose type inference. To get it back, you can use `queryOptions` helper:\n\n```ts\nimport { queryOptions } from '@tanstack/solid-query'\n\nfunction groupOptions() {\n  return queryOptions({\n    queryKey: ['groups'],\n    queryFn: fetchGroups,\n    staleTime: 5 * 1000,\n  })\n}\n\nuseQuery(groupOptions)\nqueryClient.query(groupOptions())\n```\n\nFurther, the `queryKey` returned from `queryOptions` knows about the `queryFn` associated with it, and we can leverage that type information to make functions like `queryClient.getQueryData` aware of those types as well:\n\n```ts\nfunction groupOptions() {\n  return queryOptions({\n    queryKey: ['groups'],\n    queryFn: fetchGroups,\n    staleTime: 5 * 1000,\n  })\n}\n\nconst data = queryClient.getQueryData(groupOptions().queryKey)\n//    ^? const data: Group[] | undefined\n```\n\nWithout `queryOptions`, the type of `data` would be `unknown`, unless we'd pass a generic to it:\n\n```ts\nconst data = queryClient.getQueryData<Group[]>(['groups'])\n```\n\n## Typesafe disabling of queries using `skipToken`\n\nIf you are using TypeScript, you can use the `skipToken` to disable a query. This is useful when you want to disable a query based on a condition, but you still want to keep the query to be type safe.\n\nRead more about it in the [Disabling Queries](./guides/disabling-queries.md) guide.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: typescript\ntitle: TypeScript\n---\n\nSolid Query is written in **TypeScript** to make sure the library and your projects are type-safe!\n\nThings to keep in mind:\n\n- TanStack Query follows [DefinitelyTyped's support window](https://github.com/DefinitelyTyped/DefinitelyTyped#support-window) and supports TypeScript versions released within the last 2 years. At the moment, that means TypeScript **5.6** and newer.\n- Changes to types in this repository are considered **non-breaking** and are usually released as **patch** semver changes (otherwise every type enhancement would be a major version!).\n- It is **highly recommended that you lock your solid-query package version to a specific patch release and upgrade with the expectation that types may be fixed or upgraded between any release**\n- The non-type-related public API of Solid Query still follows semver very strictly.\n\n## Type Inference\n\nTypes in Solid Query generally flow through very well so that you don't have to provide type annotations for yourself\n\n```tsx\nimport { useQuery } from '@tanstack/solid-query'\n\nconst query = useQuery(() => ({\n  queryKey: ['number'],\n  queryFn: () => Promise.resolve(5),\n}))\n\nquery.data\n//    ^? (property) data: number | undefined\n```\n\n[typescript playground](https://www.typescriptlang.org/play/?#code/JYWwDg9gTgLgBAbzgYygUwIYzQRQK5pQCecAvnAGZQQhwDkAAjBgHYDOzyA1gPRsQAbYABMAtAEcCxOgFgAUPOQR28SYRIBeFOiy4pRABQGAlHA0A+OAYTy4duGuIBpNEQBccANp0WeEACNCOgBdABo4W3tHIgAxFg8TM0sABWoQYDY0ADp0fgEANzQDAFZjeVJjMoU5aKzhLAx5Hh57OAA9AH55brkgA)\n\n```tsx\nimport { useQuery } from '@tanstack/solid-query'\n\nconst query = useQuery(() => ({\n  queryKey: ['test'],\n  queryFn: () => Promise.resolve(5),\n  select: (data) => data.toString(),\n}))\n\nquery.data\n//    ^? (property) data: string | undefined\n```\n\n[typescript playground](https://www.typescriptlang.org/play/?#code/JYWwDg9gTgLgBAbzgYygUwIYzQRQK5pQCecAvnAGZQQhwDkAAjBgHYDOzyA1gPRsQAbYABMAtAEcCxOgFgAUPOQR28SYRIBeFOiy4pRABQGAlHA0A+OAYTy4duGuIBpNEQBccANp1sHOgF0AGjhbe0ciADEWDxMzSwAFahBgNjQAOnR+AQA3NAMAVmNA0LtUgTRkGBjhLAxTCzga5jSYCABlGChgFgBzE2K5UmNjeXlwtKaMeR4eezgAPQB+UYU5IA)\n\nThis works best if your `queryFn` has a well-defined returned type. Keep in mind that most data fetching libraries return `any` per default, so make sure to extract it to a properly typed function:\n\n```tsx\nconst fetchGroups = (): Promise<Group[]> =>\n  axios.get('/groups').then((response) => response.data)\n\nconst query = useQuery(() => ({\n  queryKey: ['groups'],\n  queryFn: fetchGroups,\n}))\n\nquery.data\n//    ^? (property) data: Group[] | undefined\n```\n\n[typescript playground](https://www.typescriptlang.org/play/?ssl=11&ssc=4&pln=6&pc=1#code/JYWwDg9gTgLgBAbzgYygUwIYzQRQK5pQCecAvnAGZQQhwDkAAjBgHYDOzyA1gPRsQAbYABMAtAEcCxOgFgAUKEiw4GAB7AIbStVp01GtrLnyYRMGjgBxanjBwAvIjgiAXHBZ4QAI0Jl585Ah2eAo0GGQAC2sIWy1HAAoASjcABR1gNjQAHmjbAG0AXQA+BxL9TQA6AHMw+LoeKpswQ0SKmAi0Fnj0Nkh2C3sSnr7MiuEsDET-OUDguElCEkdUTGx8Rfik0rh4hHk4A-mpIgBpNCI3PLpGmOa6AoAaOH3DheIAMRY3UPCoprYHvJSIkpsY5G8iGMJvIeDxDnAAHoAfmm8iAA)\n\n## Type Narrowing\n\nSolid Query uses a [discriminated union type](https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/typescript-in-5-minutes-func.html#discriminated-unions) for the query result, discriminated by the `status` field and the derived status boolean flags. This will allow you to check for e.g. `success` status to make `data` defined:\n\n```tsx\nconst query = useQuery(() => ({\n  queryKey: ['number'],\n  queryFn: () => Promise.resolve(5),\n}))\n\nif (query.isSuccess) {\n  const data = query.data\n  //     ^? const data: number\n}\n```\n\n[typescript playground](https://www.typescriptlang.org/play/?#code/JYWwDg9gTgLgBAbzgYygUwIYzQRQK5pQCecAvnAGZQQhwDkAAjBgHYDOzyA1gPRsQAbYABMAtAEcCxOgFgAUKEixEKdFjQBRChTTJ45KjXr8hYgFZtZc+cgjt4kwiQC8qzNnxOAFF4CUcZwA+OC8EeTg4R2IAaTQiAC44AG06FjwQACNCOgBdABpwyKkiADEWRL8A4IAFahBgNjQAOnQTADc0LwBWXwK5Ul9feXlgChCooiaGgGU8ZGQ0NjZ-MLkIiNt7OGEsDACipyad5kKInh51iIA9AH55UmHrOSA)\n\n## Typing the error field\n\nThe type for error defaults to `Error`, because that is what most users expect.\n\n```tsx\nconst query = useQuery(() => ({\n  queryKey: ['groups'],\n  queryFn: fetchGroups,\n}))\n\nquery.error\n//    ^? (property) error: Error | null\n```\n\n[typescript playground](https://www.typescriptlang.org/play/?#code/JYWwDg9gTgLgBAbzgYygUwIYzQRQK5pQCecAvnAGZQQhwDkAAjBgHYDOzyA1gPRsQAbYABMAtAEcCxOgFgAUKEiw4GAB7AIbStVp01GtrLnyYRMGjgBxanjBwAvIjgiAXHBZ4QAI0Jl585Ah2eAo0GGQAC2sIWy1HAAoASjcABR1gNjQAHmjbAG0AXQA+BxL9TQA6AHMw+LoeKpswQ0SKmAi0Fnj0Nkh2C3sSnr7MiuEsDET-OUDguElCEkdUTGx8Rfik0rh4hHk4A-mpIgBpNCI3PLpGmOa6AoAaOH3DheIAMRY3UPCoprYHvJSIkpsY5G8iBVCNQoPIeDxDnAAHoAfmm8iAA)\n\nIf you want to throw a custom error, or something that isn't an `Error` at all, you can specify the type of the error field:\n\n```tsx\nconst query = useQuery<Group[], string>(() => ({\n  queryKey: ['groups'],\n  queryFn: fetchGroups,\n}))\n\nquery.error\n//    ^? (property) error: string | null\n```\n\nHowever, this has the drawback that type inference for all other generics of `useQuery` will not work anymore. It is generally not considered a good practice to throw something that isn't an `Error`, so if you have a subclass like `AxiosError` you can use _type narrowing_ to make the error field more specific:\n\n```tsx\nimport axios from 'axios'\n\nconst query = useQuery(() => ({\n  queryKey: ['groups'],\n  queryFn: fetchGroups,\n}))\n\nquery.error\n//    ^? (property) error: Error | null\n\nif (axios.isAxiosError(query.error)) {\n  query.error\n  //    ^? (property) error: AxiosError\n}\n```\n\n[typescript playground](https://www.typescriptlang.org/play/?#code/JYWwDg9gTgLgBAbzgYygUwIYzQRQK5pQCecAvnAGZQQhwDkAAjBgHYDOzyA1gPRsQAbYABMAtAEcCxOgFgAUKEiw4GAB7AIbStVp01GtrLnyYRMGjgBxanjBwAvIjgiAXHBZ4QAI0Jl585Ah2eAo0GGQAC2sIWy1HAAoASjcABR1gNjQAHmjbAG0AXQA+BxL9TQA6AHMw+LoeKpswQ0SKmAi0Fnj0Nkh2C3sSnr7MiuEsDET-OUDguElCEkdUTGx8Rfik0rh4hHk4A-mpIgBpNCI3PLpGmOa6AoAaOH3DheIAMRY3UPCoprYHvJSIkpsY5G8iBVCNQoPIeDxDnAAHoAfmmwAoO3KbAqGQAgupNABRKAw+IQqGk6AgxAvA4U6HQOlweGI1FA+RAA)\n\n[//]: # 'RegisterErrorType'\n\n```tsx\nimport '@tanstack/solid-query'\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/solid-query' {\n  interface Register {\n    // Use unknown so call sites must narrow explicitly.\n    defaultError: unknown\n  }\n}\n\nconst query = useQuery(() => ({\n  queryKey: ['groups'],\n  queryFn: fetchGroups,\n}))\n\nquery.error\n//    ^? (property) error: unknown | null\n```\n\n[//]: # 'RegisterErrorType'\n\n## Registering global `Meta`\n\nSimilarly to registering a [global error type](#registering-a-global-error) you can also register a global `Meta` type. This ensures the optional `meta` field on [queries](./reference/functions/useQuery.md) and [mutations](./reference/functions/useMutation.md) stays consistent and is type-safe. Note that the registered type must extend `Record<string, unknown>` so that `meta` remains an object.\n\n```ts\nimport '@tanstack/solid-query'\n\ninterface MyMeta extends Record<string, unknown> {\n  // Your meta type definition.\n}\n\ndeclare module '@tanstack/solid-query' {\n  interface Register {\n    queryMeta: MyMeta\n    mutationMeta: MyMeta\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Typing Query Options\n\nIf you inline query options into `useQuery`, you'll get automatic type inference. However, you might want to extract the query options into a separate function to share them between `useQuery` and e.g `query`. In that case, you'd lose type inference. To get it back, you can use `queryOptions` helper:\n\n```ts\nimport { queryOptions } from '@tanstack/solid-query'\n\nfunction groupOptions() {\n  return queryOptions({\n    queryKey: ['groups'],\n    queryFn: fetchGroups,\n    staleTime: 5 * 1000,\n  })\n}\n\nuseQuery(groupOptions)\nqueryClient.query(groupOptions())\n```\n\nFurther, the `queryKey` returned from `queryOptions` knows about the `queryFn` associated with it, and we can leverage that type information to make functions like `queryClient.getQueryData` aware of those types as well:\n\n```ts\nfunction groupOptions() {\n  return queryOptions({\n    queryKey: ['groups'],\n    queryFn: fetchGroups,\n    staleTime: 5 * 1000,\n  })\n}\n\nconst data = queryClient.getQueryData(groupOptions().queryKey)\n//    ^? const data: Group[] | undefined\n```\n\nWithout `queryOptions`, the type of `data` would be `unknown`, unless we'd pass a generic to it:\n\n```ts\nconst data = queryClient.getQueryData<Group[]>(['groups'])\n```\n\n## Typesafe disabling of queries using `skipToken`\n\nIf you are using TypeScript, you can use the `skipToken` to disable a query. This is useful when you want to disable a query based on a condition, but you still want to keep the query to be type safe.\n\nRead more about it in the [Disabling Queries](./guides/disabling-queries.md) guide.\n"}
